WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.060
Claire is busy with work this year, so I'm

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.980
taking over the Halloween duties.

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.260
My theme is Awesomeland.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.110
Which includes anything Phil finds awesome.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.490
It's a pretty big umbrella.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.150
Ooh, big, pretty umbrellas.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:13.280
Those are awesome.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.920
Claire loves blood and guts and gore.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.670
But who says Halloween has to be scary?

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:18.560
Everybody but

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.120
you. This is killing her.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.710
Something's dying.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.530
I don't get it. What's scary about a giant

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.220
cupcake?

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.810
We're not doing scary this year.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.250
All right, well. Heads up.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.320
We're doing crap your pants scary on account

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.150
of the contest. So I just hope we don't

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.430
offend you over here in Candyland.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.720
What contest?

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.070
Oh, it's something we started in the old

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.320
neighborhood. If you're into it, you, uh,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.930
chip in 20 bucks and scariest house on the

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.220
street wins the pot.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.930
Mm, not actual pot.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.790
I'd have to see a prescription for that.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:48.970
Wait. You're not? No.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.740
For the 12th time, I'm not a cop.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.600
Well, you're not going to offend me with

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.850
your little decorations.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.280
Please know that this is Phil.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.350
When I'm in charge. It's terrifying.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.640
Oh, I'll bet you give all the other soccer

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.590
moms a good scare with that pin that says

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:03.100
boo!

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.040
You are so lucky that I have to go to work

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.020
today. Or I would show you scary.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.510
I would win your little contest.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.310
You don't know what you're up against.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.190
We don't let preggos or people with heart

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:16.420
trouble past our front gate.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.790
A couple of years ago, we scared a man into

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.680
the hospital almost to death.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.200
Well, since you got an excuse, Princess,

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.510
looks like my winning streak will carry on.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.300
Might even win at the old house too.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:29.920
We left that place pretty scary.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.700
I'm meeting a friend for coffee.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:34.750
No you're not.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.760
No. You're helping me take this all down.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.200
Everything goes.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.940
Everything except the bunny.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.690
I have plans for the bunny.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.930
You really think it's appropriate to be

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.180
strapping your teenage daughter to a gurney?

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.500
If we win, it is.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.440
I may have to take a pee break soon.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.490
Oh, here, use this bedpan.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.800
I'm kidding. That's gross.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.190
I put candy in it here.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:03.220
Luke. Luke, I think I fell asleep.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.370
This thing is like a Temple Grandin hug.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.150
Haley, sweetie.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.400
Gowns on backwards.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.910
Oh, no. It's cuter this way.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.010
Sexy people go crazy to, you know, read a

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.480
people magazine, huh?

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.020
Phil, you're not even going to try on your

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:18.270
doctor costume.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.210
Nope. But we're going to win.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.430
Does that make you happy?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.480
Do I look happy?

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.230
You got a problem, lady?

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.070
This obsessive need to be dark and scary.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.570
You can't even stop yourself.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.110
I can stop whenever I want.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.030
Well, I'm not getting sucked in.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.670
I'm having the Halloween that I wanted.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.560
What is all this?

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.950
Is this supposed to be funny?

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.330
No, it's supposed to be scary.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.830
No, it's supposed to be awesome.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.220
You know, I

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.930
could tell that you guys didn't love us

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.070
moving in next door.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.650
Maybe because Ronnie deals pot, or maybe

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.270
because of my Confederate flag bikini.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.920
I don't know, but. But I thought we were

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.120
becoming friends.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.820
I was going to propose a joint Thanksgiving,

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.400
but this is really low.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.670
No, honey. It's okay.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.260
No, it's not okay, Ronnie.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.110
It's rude and it's cruel.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.700
I wish we had our old house so we could

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.590
drive it away as far as possible.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.980
Oh my goodness.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.350
What was that?

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.030
Uh, Amber gets touchy about this stuff.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:19.230
She. She spent six months in a cuckoo farm

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.790
in Nevada. I'm sorry.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.670
She gets mad when I say that it was in Utah.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.870
Oh my God.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.700
We had no idea, I swear.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.120
It's cool. I'll just give her a box of Cap'n

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.770
Crunch and set her in front of the fish

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.110
tank. That seems to calm her down.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:33.490
Okay.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.530
We have to shut it down, we got to shut it

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.070
down.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.030
Now, when she said joint Thanksgiving, do you

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.380
think that she meant.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.490
No. Okay.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.470
I know it's not the point, but we totally

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:49.190
would have won.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.170
I want to leave that out of your apology.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.680
Howdy, howdy. Ronnie.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:54.350
What's up?

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:55.850
Ronnie. Hi.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.530
I was looking for Amber.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:57.770
Oh.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.910
She's inside. No!

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.440
Knock it off. Amber.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.400
Amber! Hi. Listen, I wanted to apologize.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.010
I had no idea about your history, and I was

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.530
being insensitive, so I was hoping we could

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.520
